Package dbatools on a machine with PowerShell Gallery access, then copy the ZIP to the machine where you’ll run the AG script. You do not need to install it on all 12 SQL nodes. Save-Module downloads its required dbatools.library dependency too. SQL Server automation with PowerShell

On the internet-connected machine, run:
$stage = Join-Path $env:TEMP 'dbatools-offline'
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $stage -Force | Out-Null

Save-Module -Name dbatools -Path $stage

Get-ChildItem $stage   # Confirm dbatools and dbatools.library

Compress-Archive `
    -Path "$stage\dbatools", "$stage\dbatools.library" `
    -DestinationPath "$env:USERPROFILE\Desktop\dbatools-offline.zip"

Transfer dbatools-offline.zip to your DBA workstation or management server. On that destination machine, in Windows PowerShell:
$moduleRoot = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE 'Documents\WindowsPowerShell\Modules'
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $moduleRoot -Force | Out-Null

Expand-Archive -Path 'C:\Transfer\dbatools-offline.zip' `
    -DestinationPath $moduleRoot

Get-Module -ListAvailable dbatools, dbatools.library
Import-Module dbatools -ErrorAction Stop
Get-Command Invoke-DbaQuery, Copy-DbaLogin

Replace C:\Transfer\dbatools-offline.zip with the ZIP’s actual location. If Get-Module -ListAvailable returns nothing, check $env:PSModulePath -split ';' and extract both module folders into a directory listed there. Keep their version subfolders intact.






On your laptop, create and locate the ZIP:
$source = Join-Path $env:TEMP 'dbatools-offline'
Get-ChildItem $source   # Confirm dbatools and dbatools.library are both present

$zip = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE 'Desktop\dbatools-offline.zip'
Compress-Archive -Path "$source\dbatools", "$source\dbatools.library" `
    -DestinationPath $zip -Force

Get-Item $zip | Select-Object FullName, Length



Upload that .zip file from your laptop to the destination machine. On the destination, use the location where the upload actually lands:

$zip = 'C:\path\where\you\uploaded\dbatools-offline.zip'
$moduleRoot = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE 'Documents\WindowsPowerShell\Modules'

New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $moduleRoot -Force | Out-Null
Expand-Archive -LiteralPath $zip -DestinationPath $moduleRoot

Get-Module -ListAvailable dbatools, dbatools.library
Import-Module dbatools -ErrorAction Stop
Get-Command Invoke-DbaQuery, Copy-DbaLogin
